TI  - Maternal Mortality Rates in the United States, 2024.
BTI - NCHS Health E Stats
CP  - Health E-Stat 113
AB  - INTRODUCTION: This report presents maternal mortality rates in the United States 
      for 2024. METHODS: Data are from the National Vital Statistics System mortality 
      file. Maternal mortality rates are per 100,000 live births, based on data from 
      the national Vital Statistics natality file. KEY FINDINGS: The maternal mortality 
      rate for 2024 was 17.9 deaths per 100,000 live births. The rates were not 
      statistically different from 2023 overall, by age, or by race and Hispanic-origin 
      groups. The maternal mortality rates for women 40 and older were greater than 
      those for women in younger age groups. The maternal mortality rates for Black 
      non-Hispanic women were greater than those for other race and Hispanic groups.
